{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499799-exp-cost-for-humanity","id":1499799,"title":"EXP cost for Humanity","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-12-15T17:05:53-08:00","id":1499799,"title":"EXP cost for Humanity","content":"So, some of my players often tell me that they think Humanity should be sometimes awarded to players without Exp cost. What do you guys think about it? Do you agree that some actions could possibly give the PC a free/reduced cost to raise their Humanity, or do you think it should always be bought with the normal cost for raising it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T17:37:02-08:00","id":1499804,"title":"","content":"As I've said in other threads, I really don't like the &quot;waive XP&quot; approach to things. I'll try to avoid going into that too much yet again.<br /> <br /> I think part of the problem for VtM, is that Humanity really doesn't work well with the way XP costs are calculated. While the general idea of &quot;clawing your way back from the depths of depravity to normal is extremely grueling,&quot; where getting back to 7 from 3 or 4 is a lot of XP, the cost of 7 to 8 is pretty steep. It almost feels like it should be reversed so getting to high Humanity from average Humanity should be cheap (it's' easy enough to lose as it is), but trying to come back from 2-3 should be a huge deal that feels like you might never do it.<br /> <br /> I also do think you could look to the CofD 2e books for a few alternate setups where equivalent traits (not Humanity because it doesn't do this) are not changed by XP at all, and going up or down is its own system. Something about those though, is that there's a lot more consequences to smaller changes that how Humanity works. A werewolf in Forsaken 2e that moves 2 points of Harmony in either direction is going to be dealing with some major changes to their interactions with things like shapeshifting and Rage. The no-XP options in the CofD 2e tend to be less about &quot;high good, low bad&quot; and more about what rating suits the way a character acts (which might not be what they want, but then they either need to change, or wrestle with that internal conflict).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T18:06:35-08:00","id":1499813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> think part of the problem for VtM, is that Humanity really doesn't work well with the way XP costs are calculated. While the general idea of &quot;clawing your way back from the depths of depravity to normal is extremely grueling,&quot; where getting back to 7 from 3 or 4 is a lot of XP, the cost of 7 to 8 is pretty steep. It almost feels like it should be reversed so getting to high Humanity from average Humanity should be cheap (it's' easy enough to lose as it is), but trying to come back from 2-3 should be a huge deal that feels like you might never do it. </div> </div> </div>Yes, I also agree that exp cost to raise Humanity is too steep. Since I started ST, players often come to me telling me Humanity exp cost should work differently or asking me to award &quot;free&quot; Humanity points, etc. what you said makes a lot of sense, i.e. it should be harder (and thus more expensive) to raise Humanity when your Humanity is low than the other way round. The problem I often face myself is how to use another system that would be good to supplant the current one. I sometimes come to think that the way characters act should be the only thing that matter regarding Humanity, i.e. one could raise their humanity by acting consistently as someone with a higher rating, and so this way I could solve the problem with the exp costs to raise it, etc. But, then again sometimes I think such approach is a step too far. That's why I opened this discussion, I'd like to hear other's people's approach to the matter at hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T18:29:23-08:00","id":1499822,"title":"","content":"The thing is, Humanity is partially designed to fall and then stabilise at a lower rating, and to tempt the players into letting this happen. The scaling costs reinforce this, it's hard to keep your Humanity at a high level for relatively minor benefits, but if you let it fall just a couple of points it'll ping you less, and you'll have more XP to spend on other stuff...<br /> <br /> Now I don't particularly like the way Humanity is set up in Masquerade, it's all too much about being a moral person. I wouldn't bring in the Requiem 2e version though, I'd rework the concept of Roads/Paths. Not sure if Humanity would remain as 'be a good person' in that setup, I might switch it to the 'Patb of Humility' and have it be about remaining beneath noticed, I'd have to be likely to run Masquerade before I put in serious effort.<br /> <br /> I would not have good acts raise the Humanity meter, like many video game morality systems. Being a good person takes more than just the occasional good act, you've got to be consistent about it. Lots of soul-searching and soup kitchens for the penitent vampire, and if you're already quite moral it takes a lot of searching to find things to atone for.<br /> <br /> That said there are systems in CofD 2e that rely on in-game actions to raise them, but as Heavy Arms says they're structured very different to Masquerade's Humanity and meant to be potentially in more flux. Imagine if having your Humanity too high influenced your ability to use vampiric powers, it's an interesting idea but probably not what the 'free Humanity' crowd wants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T22:00:47-08:00","id":1499833,"title":"","content":"I want to change the way the system currently work, but I'm sill to find a good replacement. As I said, I've been thinking about awarding it freely/for purely narrative reasons. Besides, it's too expensive to raise Humanity and I don't really think it's fair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T22:39:13-08:00","id":1499836,"title":"","content":"I often award Humanity to PCs if they do something worthwhile for it AND they want the higher humanity. Some PCs are fine settling at a lower Humanity if that is their comfort zone for the PC, and dislike the roleplay of feeling morally bad for things they actually want to do! Some PCs prefer their humanity at 7 or 6 and others at 5 or 4. I don't force them to have higher Humanity if it gets in the way of accomplishing their goals and the means they use to do so.<br /> <br /> I also award temporary Willpower frequently as well as something beyond just XP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T23:12:40-08:00","id":1499838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499799-exp-cost-for-humanity?p=1499836#post1499836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I often award Humanity to PCs if they do something worthwhile for it AND they want the higher humanity. Some PCs are fine settling at a lower Humanity if that is their comfort zone for the PC, and dislike the roleplay of feeling morally bad for things they actually want to do! Some PCs prefer their humanity at 7 or 6 and others at 5 or 4. I don't force them to have higher Humanity if it gets in the way of accomplishing their goals and the means they use to do so.<br /> <br /> I also award temporary Willpower frequently as well as something beyond just XP.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've done it in some occasions, but never thought about creating a system for it. I just did it when I felt was right for the character and the player also wanted to have a higher humanity and was acting accordingly. Temporary Willpower I award frequently, according to the character's nature and goals, etc. Also when they rest. After a good rest, I always let them recover 1 temporary WP point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T00:03:22-08:00","id":1499841,"title":"","content":"A real simple no XP system if you don't want to make Humanity too much about XP, and want to get away from some of the strict morality aspects of it:<br /> <br /> Get rid of Humanity completely.<br /> <br /> The mechanical aspects of Humanity that deal with things like interacting with humans, or how well you can withstand weaknesses/banes is based on how full your vampire is. A completely full vampire has the appearance of a normal Humanity 10 vampire. The Beast is sated, and doesn't subconsciously freak out humans, and not hungering for blood makes it easier to focus on behaving like a human.<br /> <br /> How long things like Torpor lasts and similar mechanics that require a more stable number key off your highest Virtue instead<br /> <br /> Any time a vampire does something the violates their personal creed (make it completely individualized, or keep the Ethics of Humanity/the Paths), they risk losing a Virtue dot instead of Humanity (since Virtues only go to 5, they never get that expensive, and with three of them you can spread the damage around a bit to soften that more). The difficulty of the roll is based on how egregious the violation is rather than using the sin charts.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T04:44:11-08:00","id":1499852,"title":"","content":"Personnaly i grant my pc free humanity dots only if they accomplish something that goes against the beast.<br /> As a predator the beast is always trying to feed and unleash so each time a pc face it without loosing (make a surgery with low blood pool and resist frenzy to save a human life for exemple) he deserve to be rewarded.<br /> <br /> Resist the beast has to be very difficult, raise your humanity level should always be possible ONLY if you face it and win in a difficult struggle","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 12-16-2022, 08:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T09:33:02-08:00","id":1499859,"title":"","content":"I like it high because it explains why elders don't have better stats: they are paying what amounts to a Humanity Tax. The reason why that ancillae character only gets 35 xp is that their character-creation takes into account multiple periods when they focused on their humanity and got it back up from 4 or so. In my head-canon, any very old character has had multiple periods per century when they focused more on escaping the beast than they did the eternal political war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T10:18:18-08:00","id":1499864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499799-exp-cost-for-humanity?p=1499841#post1499841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A real simple no XP system if you don't want to make Humanity too much about XP, and want to get away from some of the strict morality aspects of it:<br /> <br /> Get rid of Humanity completely.<br /> <br /> The mechanical aspects of Humanity that deal with things like interacting with humans, or how well you can withstand weaknesses/banes is based on how full your vampire is. A completely full vampire has the appearance of a normal Humanity 10 vampire. The Beast is sated, and doesn't subconsciously freak out humans, and not hungering for blood makes it easier to focus on behaving like a human.<br /> <br /> How long things like Torpor lasts and similar mechanics that require a more stable number key off your highest Virtue instead<br /> <br /> Any time a vampire does something the violates their personal creed (make it completely individualized, or keep the Ethics of Humanity/the Paths), they risk losing a Virtue dot instead of Humanity (since Virtues only go to 5, they never get that expensive, and with three of them you can spread the damage around a bit to soften that more). The difficulty of the roll is based on how egregious the violation is rather than using the sin charts.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like this concept, especially the idea of keeping it somehow &quot;individualized&quot;, I mean the charts should only come as a sort of guideline, not a rule set in stone. I like the idea of giving characters a more individualized code, so to speak. It makes them more unique and even helps to create the character itself, in the sense of making it deeper, etc. &quot;What is important to you&quot; is a simple question that in my opinion greatly helps to build a character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T14:20:46-08:00","id":1499906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499799-exp-cost-for-humanity?p=1499859#post1499859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it high because it explains why elders don't have better stats: they are paying what amounts to a Humanity Tax. The reason why that ancillae character only gets 35 xp is that their character-creation takes into account multiple periods when they focused on their humanity and got it back up from 4 or so. In my head-canon, any very old character has had multiple periods per century when they focused more on escaping the beast than they did the eternal political war.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that the NPCs in the books aren't written based on any sort of mechanical rigor, I highly doubt this is really reflected in their stats. If anything, it seems much more likely to make PCs played long enough to be considered Elders to feel underwhelming compared to official Elder NPCs because one had to deal with this reality and the other didn't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499799-exp-cost-for-humanity?p=1499864#post1499864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this concept, especially the idea of keeping it somehow &quot;individualized&quot;, I mean the charts should only come as a sort of guideline, not a rule set in stone. I like the idea of giving characters a more individualized code, so to speak. It makes them more unique and even helps to create the character itself, in the sense of making it deeper, etc. &quot;What is important to you&quot; is a simple question that in my opinion greatly helps to build a character.</div> </div> </div> </div>CofD 2e's mortal core rules (and in a section I belief is available in the free God-Machine Rules Update pdf) has some nice guidance on helping with these sorts of things, as Integrity is also personalized to each PC through series of questions to help establish what is and isn't a major point in a character's personal journey.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T18:11:57-08:00","id":1499921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> CofD 2e's mortal core rules (and in a section I belief is available in the free God-Machine Rules Update pdf) has some nice guidance on helping with these sorts of things, as Integrity is also personalized to each PC through series of questions to help establish what is and isn't a major point in a character's personal journey. </div> </div> </div>Thank you, I'll have a look at it and see what I can adapt to my V20 games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-17T01:29:21-08:00","id":1499934,"title":"","content":"The biggest issue for me with RAW humanity is that a single high stakes dice roll can decide whether you need to pay for several sessions worth of XP to recover from that. <br /> <br /> As I run things, players can use their downtime to either<br /> A: Gain backgrounds<br /> B: Recover humanity.<br /> C: Learn rituals","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-17T03:00:01-08:00","id":1499936,"title":"","content":"Another idea is to combine Humanity and Willpower into one stat. You have your Humanity score, which mostly works as normal, but also Humanity Points that do what Willpower does. Getting back temporary Humanity is easy, but running out puts you in danger of losing actual Humanity dots.<br /> <br /> The issue is that you can't really have low-Humanity elders without making them vulnerable to things like Dominate. I'd rectify this by saying that most Elders have switched to Paths/Roads, generally at the 5-7 range, and possibly upping the difficulty of Dominate rolls, but not everybody will want that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-20T12:18:52-08:00","id":1500188,"title":"","content":"I usually award special Humanity XP (that can only be used to raise Humanity) if the Kindreds do something that is truly selfless and carries danger towards said Kindred. For example, in my campaign, the Daughter of Cacophony noticed that the house next to where her touchstone lives was on fire in the middle of the night and she was not sure if fire department would come in time to save the touchstone, so after a few rolls which she succeeded resist the fear frenzy, she ran into the flames and took quite some damage (and almost died) but she managed to rescue the person and their kid. So she was awarded some Humanity XP that she can use if she ever wants to raise humanity (but cost is still 10x current level)<br /> <br /> Also, if you do anything and lose a dot in humanity, all gathered humanity XP will be lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25995-ethryo","name":"Ethryo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-20T14:32:43-08:00","id":1500194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ethryo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499799-exp-cost-for-humanity?p=1500188#post1500188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I usually award special Humanity XP (that can only be used to raise Humanity) if the Kindreds do something that is truly selfless and carries danger towards said Kindred. For example, in my campaign, the Daughter of Cacophony noticed that the house next to where her touchstone lives was on fire in the middle of the night and she was not sure if fire department would come in time to save the touchstone, so after a few rolls which she succeeded resist the fear frenzy, she ran into the flames and took quite some damage (and almost died) but she managed to rescue the person and their kid. So she was awarded some Humanity XP that she can use if she ever wants to raise humanity (but cost is still 10x current level)<br /> <br /> Also, if you do anything and lose a dot in humanity, all gathered humanity XP will be lost.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That gave me some ideas to create a system to award Humanity to those deserving. Thank you sir.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-21T00:40:52-08:00","id":1500271,"title":"","content":"A trick I implemented was to bring touchstones from v5 as a background and each dot represented a xp reduction. <br /> <br /> I also tend to provide a reduction when you do something exceptionally decent. For example a tremere who spared a shovelheads life and smuggled her to the free states.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-21T01:25:42-08:00","id":1500272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499799-exp-cost-for-humanity?p=1500271#post1500271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A trick I implemented was to bring touchstones from v5 as a background and each dot represented a xp reduction.<br /> <br /> I also tend to provide a reduction when you do something exceptionally decent. For example a tremere who spared a shovelheads life and smuggled her to the free states.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's really nice, I like doing things similar as well, but the thing is I've never created a system for it, that's why I'm collecting ideas and thinking about a way to implement one. So that I can use it every game I storyteller. The idea for touchstone is something I'm going to analyse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-21T02:08:23-08:00","id":1500276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499799-exp-cost-for-humanity?p=1500272#post1500272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's really nice, I like doing things similar as well, but the thing is I've never created a system for it, that's why I'm collecting ideas and thinking about a way to implement one. So that I can use it every game I storyteller. The idea for touchstone is something I'm going to analyse.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I kept is pretty simple each dot lowers the xp cost by 1, I also allowed for non human stuff to be allowed on condition is can be destroyed somehow-which triggers a degeneration roll. This pretty much resolves my issues with touchstones by making them flexible and turning them from a liability into an asset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 12-21-2022, 06:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-21T04:06:15-08:00","id":1500281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ethryo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499799-exp-cost-for-humanity?p=1500188#post1500188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I usually award special Humanity XP (that can only be used to raise Humanity) if the Kindreds do something that is truly selfless and carries danger towards said Kindred. For example, in my campaign, the Daughter of Cacophony noticed that the house next to where her touchstone lives was on fire in the middle of the night and she was not sure if fire department would come in time (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Did this Vampiress later try to consider or rethink her attitude? Being pessimistic or critical of the fire fighting department or emergecy teams / crews can lead to lowered conflagration / fire preparadness, and perhaps also making minor and major mistakes when it comes to dealing with situations involving a situation with fire emergency. The ability to cooperate with other government / regime / authority / administration workers and employees could also be lowered. And choices and decisions in regard to maintaining an optimistic attitude and learning apptitudes about disasters and emergencies could be negatively impacted. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Such affairs / matters might seem prosaic, tiresome, or outright mundane, but there are various reasons why makin definite choices, and having an outlook and an approach are recommended; and can also of course definitely bring about positive outcomes and various benefits. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 12-21-2022, 07:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-21T05:19:17-08:00","id":1500287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1499799-exp-cost-for-humanity?p=1500281#post1500281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did this Vampiress later try to consider or rethink her attitude? Being pessimistic or critical of the fire fighting department or emergecy teams / crews can lead to lowered conflagration / fire preparadness, and perhaps also making minor and major mistakes when it comes to dealing with situations involving a situation with fire emergency. The ability to cooperate with other government / regime / authority / administration workers and employees could also be lowered. And choices and decisions in regard to maintaining an optimistic attitude and learning apptitudes about disasters and emergencies could be negatively impacted. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Such affairs / matters might seem prosaic, tiresome, or outright mundane, but there are various reasons why makin definite choices, and having an outlook and an approach are recommended; and can also of course definitely bring about positive outcomes and various benefits. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u201cWhen seconds count, emergency services are just minutes away.\u201d<br /> <br /> Are you seriously suggesting that the vampire take a humanity hit for not waiting to see if someone else would show up and rescue someone in time, because doubting the ability of emergency services to be everywhere all at once somehow degrades the quality of emergency services for others?<br /> <br /> If I said what I truly feel about you and your ideas I\u2019d be eating red text so I\u2019ll leave it at that.<br /> <br /> The vampire risking fire to save others definitely deserves a Humanity reward because that\u2019s above and beyond when it comes to behaving like a human* instead of a monster.<br /> <br /> Similarly, I like that concept for a Touchstone background to reduce the XP costs of Humanity. That does make it something palatable and a worthy addition to ruleset; something many high humanity vampires would naturally gravitate too even if they didn\u2019t \u201cneed\u201d it to fit the concept, while not punishing those who don\u2019t have it (it costs more to regain lost humanity, but a high conscience vampire who engaged in mostly good acts wouldn\u2019t need to make many degeneration rolls in the first place).<br /> <br /> * far from \u201chumans are bastards\u201d, studies have shown fewer than 1-in-10 will try to kill another even to save their own life without conditioning (hence the need to practically break people when training them to serve in the military), while conversely 8-in-10 will risk their own lives to save others. Thus, I\u2019d say risking yourself to save others is the epitome of humanity and the antithesis of a vampire\u2019s selfish predatory nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-22T04:55:12-08:00","id":1500365,"title":"","content":"Ambulances are saviours but they do take time and the authorities themselves advocate that you should try to give first aid before they get there if you can, Police however, even in countries with reputable police they're worse than useless for anything that is time sensitive. One time I got into a semantics argument with a dispatcher<i> while being robbed</i>, so the idea that you should put all your faith into the folks in blue sounds like a joke. <br /> <br /> <br /> Back on topic<br /> <br /> I think things like humanity should be earnable at a cost, but not XP, stuff like sacrificing a background, or sacrificing the chance to get a dot of something. <br /> <br /> One issue is that RAW conscience isn't actually a sufficient measure to reliably predict degeneration: lower amounts of dice lead to more random chance and unpredictability makes things unfair. Fleshing out the system for more dice and perhaps lower target numbers with more successes needed makes things fairer. You could perhaps do this by pairing conscience with things like academics or empathy, or perhaps run conscience AND conviction at the same time (with you putting down your convictions like a code of honour)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}